{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1452761352,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDUxNDcxMDg2MQ=="},"added":["documentation"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1452778723,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE3MTY0Njg0Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/335#issuecomment-171646843"},"message":"yeap.  Thanks for detailing it\n\nWhen we get to handles thought -- with all the rewrites for datalad's meta (thus no simple pushes of the master containing local urls, or pulls) it would be a bit more evolved ;-)  Without \"global\" urls it could've been indeed this straightforward","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1452779588,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE3MTY0OTcyOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/335#issuecomment-171649728"},"message":"So let's think again, where we need which URLs exactly.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1459971233,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIwNjUyNTIxNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/335#issuecomment-206525217"},"message":"@bpoldrack @yarikoptic Amazingly, there is no need for an API key to use the github rest API. Here is how to create a repo via python-github:\n\n```\nimport github as gh\ng=gh.Github('myusername', 'mypasswd')\nu=g.get_user()\nu.create_repo('apitest', description='some fancy', homepage='example.com')\n```\n\nThis should make `create_publication_target_github` quite a bit simpler than the sshwebserver one...\n\nCheers to the GitHub folks. Well done!","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1459971499,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIwNjUyNjU0Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/335#issuecomment-206526547"},"message":"Moreover, it supports the creation of oAuth tokens, so there is no need to store passwords....","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1459973666,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIwNjU0MDQ2MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/335#issuecomment-206540461"},"message":"sweet! works even for organizations\n\n```\n*In [5]: g = gh.Github('yarikoptic-test', '....')\n\n*In [7]: o = g.get_organization('yarikoptic-test-org')\n\nIn [8]: o.create_repo('apitest', description='some fancy', homepage='example.com')\nOut[8]: \u003cgithub.Repository.Repository at 0x7fd7880320d0\u003e\n```\n\nas for credentials, indeed could go through oauth!  I guess we should provide some centralized helper for those, otherwise could use meanwhile the Credentials contraption\n\n```\nIn [1]: from datalad.downloaders.providers import Credential\n\nIn [2]: cred = Credential('github', 'user_password', 'https://github.com/')\n\nIn [3]: creds = cred()\nYou need to authenticate with 'github' credentials. https://github.com/ provides information on how to gain access\nuser: \nYou need to authenticate with 'github' credentials. https://github.com/ provides information on how to gain access\npassword: \n\nIn [4]: print creds\n{'password': '...', 'user': 'yarikoptic-test'}\n```\n\nwhich uses keyring module, and ATM with default backend which should theoretically match the system (in my case -- gnome's)","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1476478692,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDgyNDU1MDY4Nw=="},"added":["WIP"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"3dc0514454678f1a356a3d3d9b015a3479a5351a"},"timestamp":1478822258,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1OTg0MzU3OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/335#issuecomment-259843578"},"message":"I tried the configuration reported above without success.\n\nThe main issue is that files on \"mine\" repository (the clone from github) appear to be available (with the 'whereis' command) only on [sshdata] and [public] both not accessible. The files are not indexes by [datasrc] remote. Following the example the files from local are copied on the server only to [sshdata].\nWhere am I wrong?\n\nI have an additional question. \nIt looks like the remote [httpdata] doesn't have any role.\n\nP.S. Do you have a recommendation for a docker to config git server over http? \n        I tried \"cirocosta/gitserver-http\" but it supports only bare repos.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"3dc0514454678f1a356a3d3d9b015a3479a5351a"},"timestamp":1478822544,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1OTg0NDM5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/335#issuecomment-259844391"},"message":"An additional detail. On the server the storage is mounted with sshfs.\nWhen I init the annex \"public\" I received the following notification:\n\n   init public \n  Detected a filesystem without fifo support.\n  Disabling ssh connection caching.\n  ok\n\nI don't believe it is relevant to the issue mentioned above.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486126628,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NzI0MDczMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/335#issuecomment-277240733"},"message":"Finally an update on this issue. With #1237 many things get changed (and hopefully improved). There is one more issue before this is fully resolved. Here is how the current flow is by means of a demo script. It does everything, except for the special remote setup -- which still needs some thought. Anyways, here it is:\n\n````\n#!/bin/bash -e\n\nwdir=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\ncd $wdir\n\n# fresh dataset\ndatalad create orig\ncd orig\n# remotes\n# own webserver\ndatalad --dbg create-sibling \\\n\t-s target1 \\\n\t--existing replace \\\n\t\u003cserverhostname\u003e:public_html/demoannex\n# these two are TODO for special remote setup\n#\t--as-common-datasrc ownserver \\\n#\t--target-url http://\u003cserverhostname\u003e/~user/demoannex/.git \\\n# github\ndatalad create-sibling-github \\\n\t--github-login \u003cgithubuser\u003e \\\n\t--publish-depends target1 \\\n\t--existing reconfigure \\\n\t--access-protocol ssh \\\n\tdemoannex\n\n# some new content\ntouch probe\ndatalad add probe\n\n# publish to github, which involves transfer to own server too\ndatalad publish --to github\n\n# random new user gets the new repo from from github\ncd ..\ndatalad install -s git@github.com:\u003cgithubuser\u003e/demoannex.git public\n````","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486139718,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NzI5NTU5NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/335#issuecomment-277295594"},"message":"OK, this is done (with the present state of #1237) -- just put back the two commented lines in the script above.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486139731,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDk0ODMyNzYwNQ=="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486139731,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50OTQ4MzI3NjA2"},"added":[],"removed":["WIP"]},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1486643099,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50OTU1NDgxNzIy"},"status":2}]}